flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.571084182443509%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">You may be subject to limitations on transfer of your ADSs. See &#8220;Item 3. Key Information&#8212;D. Risk Factors&#8212;Risks Related to Our ADSs and Class A Ordinary Shares&#8212;You may be subject to limitations on transfer of your ADSs&#8221; on page 68 for details; and</span></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="margin-left:6.667%;display:flex;margin-top:10pt;justify-content:flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.571084182443509%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#8226;</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">We believe that we were a passive foreign investment company, or PFIC, for U.S. federal income tax purposes for the taxable year ended December 31, 2025, and it is likely we will be a PFIC for the current taxable year and future taxable years, which could result in adverse U.S. federal income tax consequences to U.S. Holders of our ADSs. See &#8220;Item 3. Key Information&#8212;D. Risk Factors&#8212;Risks Related to Our ADSs and Class A Ordinary Shares&#8212;We believe that we were a passive foreign investment company, or PFIC, for U.S. federal income tax purposes for the taxable year ended December 31, 2025, and it is likely we will be a PFIC for the current taxable year and future taxable years, which could result in adverse U.S. federal income tax consequences to U.S. Holders of our ADSs&#8221; on page 72 for details.</span></div></div></div>
